1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,240
Last time: objects are made of materials.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,150
Glass is made from sand.

3
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:07,330
Ceramic is made from clay.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,180
Three materials to go!

5
00:00:10,652 --> 00:00:11,802
Today you'll learn:

6
00:00:12,004 --> 00:00:13,544
Wood, rubber and fabric.

7
00:00:13,748 --> 00:00:15,158
Where each one comes from.

8
00:00:15,355 --> 00:00:16,485
Count the parts.

9
00:00:17,211 --> 00:00:18,431
Lock in first.

10
00:00:18,711 --> 00:00:20,961
A little sheep is hiding in this video.

11
00:00:21,211 --> 00:00:22,451
Can you spot it?

12
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,900
First, wood.

13
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,060
This bench is made of wood.

14
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:27,610
So is your pencil.

15
00:00:29,516 --> 00:00:32,756
Wood comes from the trees in fields and forests.

16
00:00:33,494 --> 00:00:35,374
Look closer at this tree trunk.

17
00:00:35,496 --> 00:00:38,056
The trunks are cut into long, flat planks.

18
00:00:38,192 --> 00:00:39,822
See the lines in the plank?

19
00:00:40,192 --> 00:00:42,102
The bench has the same lines!

20
00:00:44,659 --> 00:00:46,519
Paper is made from wood too!

21
00:00:48,532 --> 00:00:49,412
Round one.

22
00:00:49,722 --> 00:00:52,002
The sole of this school shoe is rubber.

23
00:00:53,492 --> 00:00:55,672
Some rubber starts as white drops.

24
00:00:55,962 --> 00:00:57,252
Where do they come from?

25
00:00:57,552 --> 00:00:58,602
One, a cow.

26
00:00:58,882 --> 00:00:59,942
Two, a tree.

27
00:01:00,232 --> 00:01:01,472
Three, a rock.

28
00:01:01,752 --> 00:01:03,232
Show me with your fingers.

29
00:01:08,704 --> 00:01:09,684
Locked in!

30
00:01:09,812 --> 00:01:10,532
One!

31
00:01:10,622 --> 00:01:11,812
White drops.

32
00:01:11,902 --> 00:01:13,082
That is milk!

33
00:01:13,128 --> 00:01:14,018
Two.

34
00:01:14,188 --> 00:01:16,228
I think it is a rubber tree.

35
00:01:16,276 --> 00:01:16,906
Two!

36
00:01:17,066 --> 00:01:18,366
A rock cannot drip.

37
00:01:18,516 --> 00:01:20,056
And nobody milks a shoe!

38
00:01:20,556 --> 00:01:21,836
Be a drop of sap!

39
00:01:22,136 --> 00:01:23,126
Shrink down.

40
00:01:23,406 --> 00:01:24,336
Quietly.

41
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:30,005
You are a drop of white sap, inside a rubber tree.

42
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:32,970
Someone makes a thin cut in the bark.

43
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:34,870
You ooze out!

44
00:01:35,528 --> 00:01:38,448
You run down the cut, and drip into a little cup.

45
00:01:39,108 --> 00:01:41,648
At a factory, you are made into rubber.

46
00:01:42,307 --> 00:01:43,877
You are pressed into a shape.

47
00:01:44,677 --> 00:01:46,327
The sole of a school shoe!

48
00:01:46,991 --> 00:01:49,051
Now, you bend with every step.

49
00:01:51,461 --> 00:01:52,771
The answer is two.

50
00:01:53,041 --> 00:01:53,971
A tree!

51
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:55,852
Look closer at the cut.

52
00:01:56,232 --> 00:01:57,272
White sap!

53
00:01:57,662 --> 00:01:59,912
Drop by drop, it fills the cup.

54
00:02:00,042 --> 00:02:02,902
At the factory, the sap is made into rubber.

55
00:02:05,599 --> 00:02:06,749
Say it with me!

56
00:02:07,464 --> 00:02:09,894
Rubber can come from the sap of a rubber tree.

57
00:02:10,054 --> 00:02:13,434
It can also be made by man using oil from the ground.

58
00:02:15,842 --> 00:02:16,872
Two fingers?

59
00:02:17,142 --> 00:02:18,362
One finger up!

60
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:20,400
Last one: fabric.

61
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:22,440
Like this school T-shirt.

62
00:02:23,170 --> 00:02:24,920
Look closer at the T-shirt.

63
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,180
Threads!

64
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,520
Over, under, over, under.

65
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:30,800
Woven threads make fabric.

66
00:02:33,210 --> 00:02:37,010
Fabric is a material that can come from animals or plants.

67
00:02:38,627 --> 00:02:39,627
Round two.

68
00:02:39,917 --> 00:02:41,417
This T-shirt is cotton.

69
00:02:41,697 --> 00:02:43,197
Where does cotton come from?

70
00:02:43,507 --> 00:02:44,757
One, an animal.

71
00:02:45,057 --> 00:02:46,127
Two, a plant.

72
00:02:46,407 --> 00:02:47,887
Show me with your fingers.

73
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,340
Locked in!

74
00:02:54,468 --> 00:02:55,078
One!

75
00:02:55,208 --> 00:02:56,978
Cotton is fluffy, like a sheep!

76
00:02:57,026 --> 00:02:57,806
Two!

77
00:02:57,886 --> 00:02:59,926
Fluffy white balls, on a plant!

78
00:02:59,977 --> 00:03:00,867
Two.

79
00:03:01,017 --> 00:03:03,197
Cotton grows on a cotton plant.

80
00:03:03,473 --> 00:03:04,783
The answer is two.

81
00:03:05,053 --> 00:03:06,693
Cotton comes from a plant.

82
00:03:06,963 --> 00:03:08,413
Wool comes from sheep.

83
00:03:08,683 --> 00:03:10,773
Silk comes from a kind of caterpillar.

84
00:03:10,822 --> 00:03:11,852
Two fingers?

85
00:03:12,122 --> 00:03:13,342
One finger up!

86
00:03:13,615 --> 00:03:15,235
So sheep give wool, not cotton.

87
00:03:15,415 --> 00:03:16,505
Sorry, sheep!

88
00:03:18,083 --> 00:03:19,113
My notes!

89
00:03:19,343 --> 00:03:19,953
One.

90
00:03:20,323 --> 00:03:21,983
Wood comes from trees.

91
00:03:22,263 --> 00:03:22,993
Two.

92
00:03:23,113 --> 00:03:24,923
Glass is made from sand.

93
00:03:25,103 --> 00:03:26,013
Three.

94
00:03:26,243 --> 00:03:28,703
A school shoe is made of one material.

95
00:03:28,979 --> 00:03:29,879
Showdown!

96
00:03:30,189 --> 00:03:31,319
Double points.

97
00:03:31,589 --> 00:03:33,189
Which line has a mistake?

98
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:34,859
One, two, or three?

99
00:03:35,149 --> 00:03:36,629
Show me with your fingers.

100
00:03:43,096 --> 00:03:44,076
Locked in!

101
00:03:44,204 --> 00:03:44,894
Three!

102
00:03:45,154 --> 00:03:46,744
Let's count the parts.

103
00:03:46,790 --> 00:03:47,500
Three!

104
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:49,600
A sole, a top, and shiny rings!

105
00:03:50,028 --> 00:03:51,178
Count the parts!

106
00:03:51,548 --> 00:03:52,978
The sole: rubber.

107
00:03:53,368 --> 00:03:54,858
The top: fabric.

108
00:03:55,238 --> 00:03:56,998
The little rings: metal.

109
00:03:57,378 --> 00:03:59,218
The lace tips: plastic.

110
00:03:59,346 --> 00:04:01,376
One object, four materials!

111
00:04:01,434 --> 00:04:02,074
Oops!

112
00:04:02,584 --> 00:04:03,134
Fixed.

113
00:04:03,554 --> 00:04:04,174
Not one.

114
00:04:04,194 --> 00:04:04,614
Four!

115
00:04:05,857 --> 00:04:07,217
Showed three fingers?

116
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:09,397
Put up two more on your score hand!

117
00:04:09,899 --> 00:04:11,189
Say it with me!

118
00:04:11,897 --> 00:04:16,407
Wood, metal, ceramic, rubber, glass, plastic and fabric are some of the

119
00:04:16,427 --> 00:04:18,887
materials we use to make the things we need.

120
00:04:21,647 --> 00:04:22,752
Say it with us!

121
00:04:23,412 --> 00:04:23,842
Wood!

122
00:04:23,862 --> 00:04:24,292
Metal!

123
00:04:24,312 --> 00:04:25,259
Ceramic!

124
00:04:27,012 --> 00:04:27,811
Rubber!

125
00:04:27,912 --> 00:04:28,735
Glass!

126
00:04:30,612 --> 00:04:31,482
Plastic!

127
00:04:31,512 --> 00:04:32,415
Fabric!

128
00:04:34,212 --> 00:04:34,642
Wood!

129
00:04:34,662 --> 00:04:35,092
Metal!

130
00:04:35,112 --> 00:04:35,992
Ceramic!

131
00:04:36,012 --> 00:04:36,811
Rubber!

132
00:04:36,912 --> 00:04:37,735
Glass!

133
00:04:37,812 --> 00:04:38,682
Plastic!

134
00:04:38,712 --> 00:04:39,615
Fabric!

135
00:04:40,367 --> 00:04:41,837
Show me your score hand!

136
00:04:42,117 --> 00:04:43,227
Four fingers?

137
00:04:43,507 --> 00:04:44,507
High five!

138
00:04:45,006 --> 00:04:46,416
Did you spot the sheep?

139
00:04:46,696 --> 00:04:48,986
It was in the field, beside the trees!

140
00:04:49,256 --> 00:04:50,796
Where does wood come from?

141
00:04:51,066 --> 00:04:52,366
Tell someone at home.

142
00:04:53,155 --> 00:04:55,395
Next time, we test the materials!

143
00:04:55,675 --> 00:04:56,765
A rubber band.

144
00:04:57,055 --> 00:04:58,675
A wooden ice-cream stick.

145
00:04:58,945 --> 00:05:00,955
Which one can bend without breaking?

146
00:05:01,018 --> 00:05:02,428
Snap it, or bend it?

147
00:05:02,474 --> 00:05:03,794
Lock in your answer!

148
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:06,720
Let's read today's key words together!

149
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:07,770
Ready?

150
00:05:08,057 --> 00:05:08,667
Rubber.

151
00:05:10,066 --> 00:05:10,786
Sap.

152
00:05:11,961 --> 00:05:12,821
Fabric.

153
00:05:14,184 --> 00:05:15,124
Well done!

154
00:05:16,106 --> 00:05:17,207
Say it with us!

155
00:05:18,007 --> 00:05:18,757
Ready?

156
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:19,540
One!

157
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:20,580
two!

158
00:05:20,885 --> 00:05:22,060
Now you know!
